Project 2: Fleet Management

Object Oriented Design Process

Analysis
  Domain
    - Creates two main classes: Boat and FleetManagement (driver).
    - The fleet owns multiple boats, and the Commodore tracks maintenance spending based on purchase prices.
  Function points
    - The Commodore (actor) inputs menu commands to print, add, remove, or expense a boat.
    - The system loads data from a CSV on the first run, and loads/saves from a DB file on subsequent runs.
    - The system calculates if an expense request is allowed based on the boat's purchase price.
  Scenarios
    - System starts: checks for command line args. If CSV is present, load CSV. Else, load DB.
    - Commodore selects 'Add': inputs a comma-separated string, system parses it into a new Boat.
    - Commodore selects 'Expense': system finds boat, compares requested expense + current expense against purchase price. Rejects if total exceeds purchase price.
    - Commodore selects 'Exit': system serializes the fleet to a .db file and terminates.

Design
  Classes and objects
    - Boat (Domain entity)
    - FleetManagement (Driver/System object containing the fleet)
  Data of objects and classes
    Data of Boat class:
      - type of enum BoatType (SAILING, POWER)
      - name of type String
      - year of type int
      - makeModel of type String
      - length of type int
      - purchasePrice of type double
      - expenses of type double
    Data of FleetManagement class:
      - fleet of type ArrayList<Boat> (shared)
      - keyboard of type Scanner (shared)
      - DB_FILENAME of type String (final constant)
  Methods of objects and classes
    Method of Boat class:
      - Constructor with raw CSV string parameter
      - spendMoney(double amount) of type boolean
      - getName() of type String
      - getPurchasePrice() of type double
      - getExpenses() of type double
      - toString() of type String
    Method of FleetManagement class:
      - main
      - loadFromCSV(String filename)
      - loadFromDB()
      - saveToDB()
      - printFleet()
      - addBoat()
      - removeBoat()
      - expenseBoat()